# Tier 1 and 2 config writes, verified on hardware 2026-07-27.
# Each was written to facebd01 and read back from facebd02.
#
#   key 77 Remind      [0, 21600, 64800] -> [1, 26100, 81600]   EXACT
#   key 80 RiseSlow    [0, 10]           -> [1, 25]             EXACT
#   key  5 GCountdown  [0, 0, 1800, 1800] -> [1, 0, 600, 594]   see below
#   key 79 RiseSet     accepted, NOT READABLE, unverified
#
# GCountdown was written as [1, 0, 600, 600] and read back as
# [1, 0, 600, 594] a few seconds later: element 3 is the live remaining
# time, ticking down on the device. That is behavioural evidence the lamp
# is processing the value, not just storing it, which makes countdown the
# best-evidenced of the readback-only group.
#
# CAVEAT that keeps these honest: key 8 also read back byte-exact and
# rendered nothing. Readback proves storage, not effect. Only power,
# brightness and segments have been confirmed by SEEING the lamp change.
chime_frame: a1 18 4d 83 01 19 65 f4 1a 00 01 3e c0
gradual_frame: a1 18 50 82 01 18 19
countdown_frame: a1 05 84 01 00 19 02 58 19 02 58
riseset_frame: a1 18 4f 83 01 19 54 60 1a 00 01 27 50
